{
  "description": "The baseline every config inherits. protected_paths always route major with the security pool, and no config can turn one off or exclude a path from one. harness_paths are protected the same way: `aidd gen-docs` writes them from src/aidd/harnesses.py (every path a supported agent harness reads as instructions or runs as a hook that protected_paths does not already cover), so edit protected_paths and never harness_paths. risk_rules each validate against config.schema.json#/properties/risk_rules/items, and one with `dependencies` also fires when a diff adds a dependency it names to a manifest; a config may turn one off with `disable_rules` or narrow it with `rule_exclusions`, and its own risk_rules add to them. agent_coauthors, and agent_accounts (platform logins that are always agents, such as the accounts GitHub Copilot reviews and codes as; an approval from one never counts, `merge_approval.agent_approval`). Implicit input to every verifier.",
